message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "TCM Symptom Ontology (TCM-SO): a comprehensive bilingual ontology of Traditional Chinese Medicine symptoms with HPO / SNOMED CT / ICD-11 alignment"
abstract: >-
  A comprehensive, bilingual (Chinese/English) OWL 2 ontology of Traditional Chinese
  Medicine (TCM) symptoms. The current release (v4.13) contains 1,947 classes (1,759
  symptom classes in 34 clinical categories), bilingual labels on 100% of classes,
  English textual definitions for 93.1% of symptom classes (50.4% manually
  translated), 15,796 existential restrictions and 20 equivalence axioms providing
  GO-style faceted classification. Cross-terminology alignment, confirmed by TCM
  domain experts, covers 649 HPO, 707 SNOMED CT and 973 ICD-11 mappings; 979 of
  1,758 symptom classes (55.7%) align to at least one external terminology.
  Logical consistency verified with the HermiT reasoner (0 unsatisfiable classes).
